                    "linkHoverColor": "#514293",
                    "linkUnderline": true,
                    "linkHoverUnderline": true
                  },
                  "text": "Rain is slightly acidic. As it runs over rock, it dissolves tiny amounts of minerals and carries them downhill. Each river brings only a little, but it has been doing this for a very long time. Water leaves the sea as vapour; the minerals have nowhere to go.",
